UID:83e3b89380333baa674f11ce731a9a68@wheeling-events
DTSTAMP:20260727T132255Z
SUMMARY:Heritage Music BluesFest
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260807
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260810
DESCRIPTION:Location: Heritage Port\, 1201 Water Street\, Wheeling\, WVDa
 tes: August 7\,8\,9\, 2026 ​​ Festival Hours & Schedule Friday Gates:
  VIP & Canopy Spot: 2:00 PM General Admission: 3:30 PM Saturday & Sunday:
  Gates open at 10:30a Stages: Performances take place on the Main Stage a
 nd the Second Stage with minimal overlap. AfterJam: Each night\, join the
  official AfterJam at Waterfront Hall from 11:00 PM – 1:00 AM. VIPs get
  in free Daily Lineup & Schedule: Will be released June 1\, 2026 on our w
 ebsite and social media. ​Tickets & Entry Ticketing: Refer to the Ticke
 ting Page for pricing and availability. Single Day & On-Site Tickets: Ava
 ilable during the festival but at higher prices. Re-Entry: Allowed with y
 our wristband. Refunds: No refunds for weather or unforeseen circumstance
 s. Wristbands: Lost or damaged wristbands cannot be replaced—please tre
 at them like cash. ADA Access: ADA tickets are available for those in whe
 elchairs\, including accessible restrooms and viewing areas. Please email
  us at live@waterfronthall.com to make arrangements. ​Parking & Transpo
 rtation Parking Garages: The Intermodal Garage at 1401 Main St\, Wheeling
 \, WV 26003 (1 minute walk) The Market Street Garage on the Corner of Mar
 ket Street and 11th (4 minute walk) The 10th Street Garage on the Corner 
 of 10th and Market Street. (7 minute walk) Street Parking There will be a
 mple street parking within a 10 minute walk of the festival. ​​ Hotel
  Shuttles: Our goal is to provide free shuttles to and from all partner h
 otels. We will update the website accordingly with new information. Taxi/
 Uber/Lyft: Dropoff/Pickup will be on the corner of Main Street & 12th Str
 eet. Bicycle Parking: Racks available outside Waterfront Hall. RVs & Camp
 ers: Please email us directly at live@waterfronthall.com if you’re cons
 idering bringing a pull-behind camper or RV— we don't have a site for y
 ou yet\, but we’d love to talk. ​ ​Lodging & Camping Guests are enc
 ouraged to stay at one of our partner hotels. Hotel Shuttles: Our goal is
  to provide free shuttles to and from all partner hotels. We will update 
 the website accordingly with new information. There is no on-site camping
  in 2026. Our goal is to offer camping within walking distance of the fes
 tival grounds in 2027. ​ Food & Beverage Expect some of the best cuisin
 e in our region. Beer\, wine\, and spirits will be sold on-site in 2026. 
 Plenty of non-alcoholic beverage selections\, vegan\, and vegetarian food
  options will be available. Water refill stations will be provided throug
 hout the festival grounds. Refillable water bottles are allowed. Small\, 
 clear\, soft-sided coolers with snacks and water are permitted. Outside a
 lcohol is strictly prohibited. ​ ​Family & Kids Children under 18 mus
 t be accompanied by a guardian. Kids under 12 get in free. GA Access Only
  Strollers are permitted. ​ ​Pets & Service Animals Only service anim
 als with proper paperwork are allowed. We love them\, but please do not b
 ring pets\, emotional support animals\, or other animals to the festival.
  ​ ​Weather & Safety Bluesfest is a rain or shine event. We are all t
 aking the risk together. In the event of severe weather\, additional exit
  gates will be opened to allow quick return to nearby parking garages. We
  also recommend seeking shelter at Waterfront Hall if weather conditions 
 are adverse. Follow on-site announcements and official social media for r
 eal-time updates. ​ ​Prohibited Items To ensure everyone’s safety a
 nd comfort: No glass containers No weapons No drones or fireworks No larg
 e umbrellas Only 10x10 canopies are allowed for those who bought one of t
 he 38 canopy spaces. Only clear bags and backpacks permitted into the fes
 tival No outside alcohol email us at live@waterfronthall.com with any que
 stions related to prohibited items not listed. ​ ​ Festival Services 
 Lost & Found: Located at the Main Entrance Tent. First Aid: Staffed medic
 al tent available near the main stage area. Water Stations: Multiple refi
 ll points located throughout the grounds. Merch Booth: Official Bluesfest
  merchandise will be available for purchase. Volunteer\, Vendor\, and Spo
 nsor Info: Registration closes May 1\, 2026. Learn more on our website un
 der “Get Involved.” ​ ​Still Have Questions? Email: live@waterfro
 nthall.comFollow us on Instagram and Facebook for updates.\nCategories: F
 estivals\, Music\, Outdoors\nSource: https://wheelingcvb.com/events/herit
 age-music-bluesfest/
LOCATION:Wheeling Heritage Port\, 1201 Water Street\, Wheeling\, WV 26003
URL:https://wheelingcvb.com/events/heritage-music-bluesfest/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
