 ic. Folks are welcome to attend either as a musical participant or just c
 ome and enjoy dinner while you listen. Also from 5-6pm\, more experienced
  musicians will be available to provide free instruction on any of the st
 andard bluegrass instruments and vocal skills to enable you to get starte
 d in Bluegrass music or enhance an existing skill level. Especially welco
 me\, are young musicians. Those getting instruction are then welcome to s
 tay and participate in the jam. Folks can text or call Bob @ 304-281-6148
  for information about adult instructions\, young students or anything el
 se pertaining to the jam. *Holiday Mondays are considered Memorial Day\, 
 4th of July\, Labor Day and also Thanksgiving eve or day\, Christmas eve 
 or day or New Years eve or day that falls on a Monday.\nSchedule note: Ev
