BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:83e7a7125c1dff0cbe62fce4fd696f0a@wheeling-events
DTSTAMP:20260727T132255Z
SUMMARY:Dwight Yoakam
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260827T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260827T213000
DESCRIPTION:Dwight Yoakam is a legendary artist whose influence has resha
 ped the landscape of country music and beyond. With over 25 million album
 s sold worldwide\, he is a 21-time GRAMMY® nominee and multiple GRAMMY®
  Award winner. His catalog includes 12 gold albums and 9 platinum or mult
 i-platinum releases\, with five topping Billboard Country Albums chart an
 d 14 landing in the Top 10. Nearly 40 of his singles have charted on Bill
 board\, including 14 Top 10 hits. A recipient of the Americana Music Asso
 ciation’s Artist of the Year award and BMI Country Music’s President
 ’s Award\, the highest honors bestowed by each organization\, Yoakam wa
 s also inducted into the Nashville Songwriters Hall of Fame in 2019. His 
 latest release\, Brighter Days (Via Records/Thirty Tigers)\, marks his fi
 rst new album in nine years. Released in November 2024\, the album was wr
 itten and recorded over a three-year period and features twelve brand-new
  songs written or co-written by Yoakam. It also includes three seemingly 
 disparate covers: “Keep On the Sunny Side” by the Carter Family\, “
 Bound Away” by Cake\, and “Time Between” by Chris Hillman of The By
 rds\, artfully woven into the same body of work in the unmistakable style
  that could only be Dwight Yoakam. A passionate curator of musical herita
 ge\, Yoakam launched his SiriusXM channel Dwight Yoakam and The Bakersfie
 ld Beat: Where Country Went Mod in 2018\, spotlighting the Bakersfield so
 und and its far-reaching influence. The channel celebrates the Bakersfiel
 d sound and those whom it has inspired. Guests have included Post Malone\
 , Lukas Nelson\, Beck\, Chris Hillman\, Jakob Dylan\, and Jackie DeShanno
 n. In 2016\, Yoakam released Swimmin’ Pools\, Movie Stars...\, on Sugar
  Hill Records. Featuring a band of bluegrass luminaries\, this album boas
 ts a collection of reinterpreted favorites from his catalogue\, as well a
 s a cover of Prince’s “Purple Rain”. Produced by nine-time GRAMMY®
  winner Gary Paczosa (Alison Krauss\, Dolly Parton)\, Jon Randall (songwr
 iter of “Whiskey Lullaby”)\, and Yoakam himself\, and mixed by Chris 
 Lord-Alge\, this album reflects the love for bluegrass music that Yoakam 
 developed at an early age in Kentucky and that has inspired him for many 
 years thereafter. In 2018\, Yoakam released two songs\, “Pretty Horses
 ” and “Then Came Monday” (the latter written with Chris Stapleton).
  Yoakam is a multifaceted artist\, seamlessly blending his musical talent
 s with a robust acting career. He has appeared in over 40 feature films\,
  including notable roles in Sling Blade (1996) and Panic Room (2002). He 
 later reunited with Billy Bob Thornton for David E. Kelley’s Amazon ser
 ies Goliath. Yoakam portrayed Warden Burns in Steven Soderbergh's Logan L
 ucky (2017) alongside Channing Tatum and Daniel Craig and took on the rol
 e of Howard Polk in Clint Eastwood's Cry Macho (2021). Throughout his car
 eer\, he has demonstrated his acting range alongside acclaimed actors suc
 h as Jodie Foster\, Tommy Lee Jones\, Jared Leto\, Forest Whitaker\, and 
 Matthew McConaughey. Whether on stage\, in the studio\, or on screen\, Yo
 akam continues to evolve as one of the most compelling and culturally sig
 nificant artists of our time.\nSchedule note: One Day Only\nCategories: C
 apitol Theatre\, Music\nSource: https://wheelingcvb.com/events/dwight-yoa
 kam/
LOCATION:Capitol Theatre\, 1015 Main Street\, Wheeling\, WV 26003
URL:https://wheelingcvb.com/events/dwight-yoakam/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:05e7c22e364fce673bc281663c64cf08@wheeling-events
DTSTAMP:20260727T132255Z
SUMMARY:Jam Night
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260827T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260827T220000
DESCRIPTION:Join Ohio Valley Gigs every Thursday night for the premier mu
 sician’s jam session at the historic Waterfront Hall. Whether you are a
  seasoned pro looking to network or a rising talent ready to take the sta
 ge for the first time\, this is the place to connect with the local music
  community. The SetupLeave the heavy lifting to us! We provide a full pro
 fessional stage equipped with:Full drum kitGuitar and bass amplifiers pia
 no.Professional PA system and microphones How to PlayThe night is designe
 d for maximum flexibility. You can:Perform Solo: Show off your latest ori
 ginal or a favorite cover.Bring Your Band: Get some stage time with your 
 full group.Jam with the Pros: Don't have a band? Our talented House Band 
 is on standby to sit in and back you up on any style—from blues and roc
 k to jazz and country. Networking & CommunityThis isn't just a concert\; 
 it’s a hub for the Ohio Valley music scene. Use this night to meet pote
 ntial bandmates\, book future gigs\, and support your fellow local artist
 s in a collaborative\, high-energy environment. What to Bring: Just your 
 instrument (guitar\, bass\, horns\, etc.) and your talent! Admission is f
 ree for performers and spectators. Come for the music\, stay for the comm
 unity.\nSchedule note: Every Thursday\nCategories: Music\nSource: https:/
 /wheelingcvb.com/events/jam-night/
LOCATION:Waterfront Hall\, 1230 Water Street\, Wheeling\, WV 26003
URL:https://wheelingcvb.com/events/jam-night/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
