BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:460892cad5b5414799e75362381ddd53@wheeling-events
DTSTAMP:20260727T132255Z
SUMMARY:An Evening with Jay Leno
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260926T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260926T213000
DESCRIPTION:Acclaimed late-night television host\, stand-up comedian\, be
 st-selling author\, car enthusiast\, and philanthropist\, Jay Leno remain
 s one of the most recognizable and respected figures in American entertai
 nment. Known for his tireless work ethic and quick wit\, Leno has long be
 en described as “the hardest working man in show business.” Leno domi
 nated late-night television for two decades as host of NBC’s “The Ton
 ight Show with Jay Leno.” During his tenure\, the show consistently ran
 ked as the #1 late-night program in the ratings. His legendary run cement
 ed his place as one of the most successful hosts in television history. T
 oday\, Leno continues to perform comedy shows each year\, touring theater
 s\, casinos\, and performing arts centers across the United States and in
 ternationally. His live act combines observational humor\, storytelling\,
  and current events\, delivered with the same approachable style that mad
 e him a household name. A lifelong automotive enthusiast\, Leno remains d
 eeply involved in the car world through his popular “Jay Leno’s Garag
 e” digital series and YouTube channel\, where he explores rare\, histor
 ic\, and cutting-edge vehicles while highlighting the people behind them.
  The series grew from his personal passion into a globally followed autom
 otive platform with millions of fans. He is also the creator of Jay Leno
 ’s Garage Advanced Vehicle Care\, a widely respected automotive product
  line used by collectors and enthusiasts around the world. Beyond comedy 
 and cars\, Leno has lent his voice to numerous animated films and televis
 ion projects\, authored children’s books\, written automotive columns\,
  and hosted television programs including the revival of the classic game
  show “You Bet Your Life.” Throughout his career\, Leno has received 
 numerous honors including Emmy Awards\, People’s Choice Awards\, the Ma
 rk Twain Prize for American Humor\, the Hasty Pudding Man of the Year Awa
 rd from Harvard University\, and a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame. He
  has also been recognized by the Congressional Medal of Honor Society wit
 h the Patriot Award for his dedication to supporting U.S. service members
  and veterans. When not performing or filming\, Leno spends much of his t
 ime working on his legendary collection of classic cars and motorcycles\,
  widely regarded as one of the most impressive private collections in the
  world. Jay and his wife Mavis\, a longtime human rights activist\, resid
 e in Los Angeles.\nSchedule note: One Day Only\nCategories: Capitol Theat
 re\, Comedy\nSource: https://wheelingcvb.com/events/an-evening-with-jay-l
 eno/
LOCATION:Capitol Theatre\, 1015 Main Street\, Wheeling\, WV 26003
URL:https://wheelingcvb.com/events/an-evening-with-jay-leno/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
