BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:633f1c1161b0dec82f59a96bf6e801eb@wheeling-events
DTSTAMP:20260727T132255Z
SUMMARY:Broadway on Main Street: "The Music Man"
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261007T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261007T213000
DESCRIPTION:There's trouble in River City when a fast-talking salesman ge
 ts his heart stolen by the town librarian. Meredith Willson's six-time\, 
 Tony Award-winning musical comedy The Music Man follows fast-talking trav
 eling salesman\, Harold Hill\, as he cons the people of River City\, Iowa
 \, into buying instruments and uniforms for a boys' band that he vows to 
 organize — this\, despite the fact he doesn't know a trombone from a tr
 eble clef. His plans to skip town with the cash are foiled when he falls 
 for Marian\, the librarian\, who transforms him into a respectable citize
 n by curtain's fall. Featuring songs such as "Seventy-Six Trombones\," "T
 rouble\," "Til There Was You\," "Pickalittle" and "Gary\, Indiana\," The 
 Music Man is a family-friendly story to be shared with every generation.\
 nSchedule note: One Day Only\nCategories: Capitol Theatre\, Theater\nSour
 ce: https://wheelingcvb.com/events/broadway-on-main-street-the-music-man/
LOCATION:Capitol Theatre\, 1015 Main Street\, Wheeling\, WV 26003
URL:https://wheelingcvb.com/events/broadway-on-main-street-the-music-man/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
