BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:295c77881a6155de237821b62b567b2f@wheeling-events
DTSTAMP:20260727T132255Z
SUMMARY:Writers Association of Northern Appalachia 2026 Writers Conferenc
 e
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DESCRIPTION:Please join us in beautiful Wheeling Park in Wheeling\, West 
 Virginia for the Writers Association of Northern Appalachia’s Annual Co
 nference October 16-17\, 2026. What’s New this Year? Regular WANA atten
 dees have come to expect an informative\, relaxed gathering in the hills 
 of Northern Appalachia. That hasn’t changed. In fact\, it’s gotten ev
 en better! This year WANA will take place in beautiful Wheeling Park\, a 
 406-acre West Virginia gem with roots as a 1900s amusement park. Since 19
 25\, it’s offered year-round recreation\, scenic beauty\, and a deep se
 nse of community. The conference will be held in its newly renovated Whit
 e Palace\, which functions as a conference center and banquet hall. We wi
 ll make use of the grounds\, including Good Lake and the picnic shelters\
 , as part of our conference experience. Learn more about the park here: h
 ttps://oglebay.com/explore/wheeling-park/ In addition to sessions on craf
 t\, the business of writing\, generative workshops\, and more\, we have a
 dded an environmental writing track that will make use of the park ground
 s\, which will be stunning in mid-October. In all\, we will offer partici
 pants more than 25 sessions that will help energize us all for the winter
  writing months ahead. This year’s open mic will be held at Wheeling’
 s newest venue\, Esoterica. (Read more about this labor of love here.) Th
 e evening will be kicked off by a collage reading celebrating 40 years of
  Bottom Dog Press led by retiring press founder\, Larry Smith. After a br
 ief intermission\, we will invite writers up to read their own work (with
  a strict two-minute time limit). Of course\, we are thrilled to welcome 
 Amy Jo Burns as this year’s keynote speaker. Her latest book\, Wait for
  Me\, is a New York Times Bestseller. She will be on hand to sign books b
 efore and after her presentation. And if you like the music of the novel\
 , we have a surprise for you\, but you’ll have to wait and see. Finally
 \, the other new piece of this year’s conference is a post-conference h
 angout. The conference will wrap up around 5 pm on Saturday\, October 16.
  For those of you who want to skedaddle back home or explore Wheeling (mo
 re info about Wheeling will be provided in the program and on our website
 )\, this gives you plenty of time to track down some dinner and be on you
 r way. But\, for those of you who want one last chat with a new friend yo
 u met at the conference or to volunteer for next year\, we will be gather
 ing in the shelter above the park for non-alcoholic libations and snacks 
 (provided by WANA)\, and you are welcome to BYOB. (There’s more than a 
 few stores nearby to pick up your favorite beverages.) We are looking for
 ward to this laid-back\, agenda-free\, after-conference gathering\, and w
 e hope you will join us. Why Attend WANA? In addition to offering attende
 es a wealth of new writing ideas\, strategies for publishing your work\, 
 and so much more\, WANA wants all of you to feel at home. Unlike other wr
 iting conferences that may seem impersonal or highfalutin’ (yeah\, we l
 ove that word)\, WANA strives to be a welcoming gathering of writers thro
 ughout the region who genuinely want to support each other through the hi
 ghs and lows of the writing life. Whether you are writing your first nove
 l or have published your fifth book of poetry\, there’s a place for you
  at WANA. Please join us. And don’t forget . . . In addition to your ch
 oice of over 20 sessions\, an open mic\, the Bottom Dog Press reading\, a
 nd an inspiring keynote\, you will have access to our exhibit hall\, whic
 h will be bigger and more diverse than ever\, have the option to join us 
 for a catered lunch (or have lunch on your own)\, and so much more.\nCate
 gories: Educational\nSource: https://wheelingcvb.com/events/writers-assoc
 iation-of-northern-appalachia-2026-writers-conference/
LOCATION:Wheeling Park\, 1801 National Road\, Wheeling\, WV 26003
URL:https://wheelingcvb.com/events/writers-association-of-northern-appala
 chia-2026-writers-conference/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
