BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7d02a25addb25c5c1e3bdfc062651dc4@wheeling-events
DTSTAMP:20260727T132255Z
SUMMARY:Wheeling Symphony Orchestra: "An Afternoon in Spain"
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270213T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270213T180000
DESCRIPTION:Escape the dreary cold of February for an afternoon in invigo
 rating Spain\, with music that evokes the spirit\, color\, and landscape 
 of Spanish life. The concert opens with Rimsky-Korsakov’s Capriccio Esp
 agnol\, a joyful\, festive work inspired by Spanish folk dances\, conduct
 ed by WSO Associate Conductor Yoona Jeong. We then continue with Leanna P
 rimiani’s Visions\, a new work commissioned through the prestigious Vir
 ginia B. Toulmin Foundation. From there\, we return to Spain for Manuel d
 e Falla’s Nights in the Gardens of Spain\, featuring the Wheeling premi
 ere performance of exciting young pianist Natalia Kazaryan. Written in th
 ree movements\, each named for a specific Spanish garden\, the piece take
 s listeners on an evocative journey\, showcasing the orchestra with the s
 ame richness and imagination as the solo piano. To close the concert\, we
  return to the music of Leanna Primiani with her Triptych\, a work origin
 ally inspired by Wheeling’s own Betty Zane.\nSchedule note: One Day Onl
 y\nCategories: Capitol Theatre\, Music\nSource: https://wheelingcvb.com/e
 vents/wheeling-symphony-orchestra-an-afternoon-in-spain/
LOCATION:Capitol Theatre\, 1015 Main Street\, Wheeling\, WV 26003
URL:https://wheelingcvb.com/events/wheeling-symphony-orchestra-an-afterno
 on-in-spain/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
