BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:dc54f4449c954c8f73f6d6a6341b32ff@wheeling-events
DTSTAMP:20260727T132255Z
SUMMARY:Broadway on Main Street: "Dr. Seuss's The Cat in the Hat"
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270329T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270329T200000
DESCRIPTION:The kids are bored... again. What to do with YOUR Thing One a
 nd Thing Two?! Here's an idea: Bring the whole family to the World's Numb
 er 1 The Cat in The Hat show for an experience they'll never forget. The 
 story has been around for over 50 years and kids still love it... just li
 ke you did! Two bored kids (this was way before iPads). One rainy day (we
 've all had a few of those)\, and one crazy cat wearing a red-striped hat
  (where was the background check for that babysitter?!). In 1957\, Dr. Se
 uss used only 200 words to write his classic tale. More than 50 years lat
 er\, The Cat in The Hat is a much-loved children's phenomenon. The play w
 as adapted for the stage in 2009 by the National Theatre of Britain. The 
 Cat in The Hat interrupts this rainy afternoon with his unexpected visit 
 to Sally and her brother's cozy home. Their outspoken and outraged pet Fi
 sh is astounded and concerned\, but this cat will not be deterred. He wil
 l teach us all to make our own fun with nothing but a little imagination.
  "It's fun to have fun\, but you have to know how." Along with Thing One 
 and Thing Two\, the cat will fill the theatre with mischievous humour and
  madcap style. A timeless tale with a twist — this energetic adaptation
  bursts onto the stage (and maybe the aisles). Expect laughs\, surprises\
 , and just a bit of delightful disorder!\nSchedule note: One Day Only\nCa
 tegories: Capitol Theatre\, Theater\nSource: https://wheelingcvb.com/even
 ts/broadway-on-main-street-dr-seusss-the-cat-in-the-hat/
LOCATION:Capitol Theatre\, 1015 Main Street\, Wheeling\, WV 26003
URL:https://wheelingcvb.com/events/broadway-on-main-street-dr-seusss-the-
 cat-in-the-hat/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7ac57cf12a0d84c7e1d11d20e7c12581@wheeling-events
DTSTAMP:20260727T132255Z
SUMMARY:Wheeling Symphony Orchestra: "Ode To Joy"
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270430T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270430T213000
DESCRIPTION:Our Masterworks season comes to an exciting close with Ode to
  Joy\, the inspiration behind our season title. After two seasons of coll
 aborating with the Wheeling Symphony Community Choir\, we are thrilled th
 is year to introduce them officially as the Wheeling Symphony Chorus\, a 
 core part of WSO performances. Beethoven’s Symphony No. 9 was selected 
 with the chorus in mind\, bringing them back to the stage as a central pa
 rt of our Capitol Series. In addition\, the choir will be joined by four 
 talented soloists: Monica Yunus\, Marianne Cornetti\, Victor Cadamone\, a
 nd Alan Cline. The WSO will also perform Brahms’s Academic Festival Ove
 rture\, a joyful collection of German student songs that shows Brahms at 
 his most festive. We round out the program with the thrilling world premi
 ere of Will Dixon’s Les Belles de Lausanne. Dixon was a Black Wheeling 
 native who went on to great musical success in New York City\, but whose 
 history and legacy have largely been forgotten. It is our honor to help b
 ring Dixon’s work back into the spotlight. His life\, career\, and rema
 rkable Wheeling roots will also serve as the subject of this year’s Fes
 tival of Ideas.\nSchedule note: One Day Only\nCategories: Capitol Theatre
 \, Music\nSource: https://wheelingcvb.com/events/wheeling-symphony-orches
 tra-bohemian-spirit/
LOCATION:Capitol Theatre\, 1015 Main Street\, Wheeling\, WV 26003
URL:https://wheelingcvb.com/events/wheeling-symphony-orchestra-bohemian-s
 pirit/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
